  "final_message": "I wrote `answer.json` with four functions in the `billing` package that emit `subscription.updated` directly. All four are in `billing/subscriptions.py`:\n\n- `subscriptions.transition` emits it for every status change except to `canceled`, which emits `subscription.canceled` instead.\n- `subscriptions.change_items` emits it after the items are swapped.\n- `subscriptions.cancel` emits it when cancellation is scheduled for period end.\n- `subscriptions.reactivate` emits it when a scheduled cancellation is undone.\n\nCallers further up, such as `pause`, `resume` and the full-cancel path, reach the event only through `transition`, so I left them out. I found no other `subscription.updated` emitters in the package. I didn't run the tests or mypy, since I only read code and wrote the answer file.",
